hexagon: store the rows of dst in the tiled HVX matmul, not the padded weight rows
Fold-into: upstream/hexagon-host

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

Tasks #175 and #178 of fuzz-ops: the tiled HVX matmul writes past its
output. The tiled kernels of htp/matmul-ops.c get the count of rows to store
for each tile of 32 weight rows from ne01 of the weight (src_w->ne[1] in the
two MUL_MAT_ID forms). For a repacked weight the host sends ne[1] rounded up
to a multiple of 32. When the real row count is not a multiple of 32, the
last tile stores up to 31 values past the end of each row of dst.

This patch gets the count of rows to store from ne[0] of dst in the five
tiled kernels. The weights of the Qwen3.5 models on the phone have row
counts that are multiples of 32, thus their results do not change. The same
change is in the diagnosis of fuzz-ops
(build/fuzz/ops/fixes/htp-tiled-store-rows-from-dst.patch).

Evidence (2026-09-23):
- The DSP libraries for v73, v75, v79 and v81 build with this patch. The
  kernel lab (tools/htp-lab) calls the tiled dot kernels with the count of
  rows as an argument (lab/target_q8.c). No lab target runs the loops of
  matmul-ops.c that this patch changes. Task #123 holds the missing lab
  targets.
- The phone check of the five patches of fuzz-hexhost together (OnePlus 13,
  the 2B Q8_0 on HTP0, thermal status 0, cpu7 cap 4.32 GHz, battery 27.6 to
  27.7 °C, MemAvailable 8.9 to 9.5 GB):
  - test-backend-ops on HTP0, the MUL_MAT_ID cases (390 cases): pass before
    and after. The four other op groups also pass before and after.
  - llama-bench tg32 -r 3 after one warmup at 23.76 t/s: before 23.56 ±
    0.10, after 23.59 ± 0.27, before 23.63 ± 0.13, after 23.57 ± 0.11 t/s.
  - llama-speculative-simple with the MTP draft of depth 4, temperature 0,
    64 tokens: before 23.589 and 23.685 t/s, after 24.076 and 24.029 t/s.
    Each run accepts 44 drafts (52.381 %), and the four runs give the same
    text. Thus the DSP library of this patch runs the real generation, and
    the output does not change.

Measurement: the patch changes the value that each tile loop reads, not the
count of operations. The tg32 of the phone check does not change.

